":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Tosafot names Yehudah and Neḥemyah as Akiva’s students and cites Yevamot.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Rabbah includes Neḥemyah in the alternate group of seven later pupils.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Neḥemyah transmits the fire and mule tradition in his father’s name.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Akiva asks Neḥemyah about the force of “one.”","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The next unit gives the two together in the oil measure dispute.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The same pair appears in the ritual dispute about the top of the altar.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The two are named together in the interest-baraita exemption.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Neḥemyah and Elazar give an oil-measure ruling. Compare the Eliezer ben Yaakov naming in Sifra before interpreting the name.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The digital Rabbah has Eliezer son of Yose the Galilean, where Heilprin writes Elazar. Preserve both.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Neḥemyah and Yehudah are named as disputants; the two views are anonymous individually.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Yerushalmi lists all seven in the same sequence and fixes the location as the Rimon valley.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The exact internal target reports this same intercalation assembly.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The cited digital Nedarim 4:3 names Eliezer, but does not give a Neḥemyah statement. The surrounding chapter also does not supply a secure replacement. Preserve the printed locator.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Middot has no folio 11 in the standard structure. The neighboring Makkot 11 dispute is independently verified. No further locus is established.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Checked Eruvin 5 does not show this disagreement. Eruvin 35a cites the two together on the same side. Check whether Heilprin had another locus before making a link.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"A separately transmitted Seder Tannaim rule has the same result, but the cited Yemot Olam gate 3 witness was not available for direct collation. Keep the reported source and keep it unlinked.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Terumot 8:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Terumot_8.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Maasrot 3:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Maasrot_3.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Shabbat 8:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Shabbat_8.4"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Shabbat 17:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Shabbat_17.4"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Yevamot 5:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Yevamot_5.6"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Nedarim 3:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Nedarim_3.11"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Nazir 9:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Nazir_9.4"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.4"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Sanhedrin 1:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sanhedrin_1.6"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Sanhedrin 9:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sanhedrin_9.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Sanhedrin 10:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sanhedrin_10.3"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Zevachim 13:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Zevachim_13.6"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Niddah 9:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Niddah_9.3"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Zavim 4:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Zavim_4.3"},